  "worked_solution": "To estimate the price of each of the $6$ perfumes, we need to find an approximation for $90.33÷6.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n90.33\\to 90\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $90$ by $6$ as usual:\n\n$$\n90÷6=15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the approximate price for each bottle is $$15.$",
